# TSX Readability

## Conditional expressions

- Avoid nested ternary expressions inside JSX props or render trees.
- If JSX value logic needs more than one condition, compute it in named `const` values or a small helper before `return`.
- Prefer a clear sequence (`baseValue` -> `overrideValue` -> `displayValue`) over inline branching.
- Keep JSX attributes simple: pass identifiers, not complex inline expression blocks.

## Repeated formatting and fallback logic

- When the same fallback/normalization logic appears in more than one field, extract a local helper or shared helper.
- Use explicit names that describe intent (`resolveRowDateValue`, `normalizedValue`) instead of re-encoding logic in-place.
